    {
      "revision": 2,
      "summary": "The page tells the host how it looks: set-appearance drives the status bar, and splash-shown says the web splash has painted. Both are sends, so an older host logs them rather than hanging — but a bundle gated on the appearance channel would leave the clock unreadable on a host that ignores it.",
      "adds": {
        "ios": [
          "set-appearance",
          "splash-shown"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "revision": 3,
      "summary": "Android answers the over-the-air update channels, so the shared update modal works on mobile. \"Install\" rebuilds the WebView rather than restarting anything — see homerun-mobile/docs/ota-bundles.md.",
      "adds": {
        "android": [
          "wait-for-update-check",
          "quit-and-install"
        ],
        "ios": []
      }
    },
    {
      "revision": 4,
      "summary": "Android answers the two system-chrome channels. set-appearance sets the status-bar glyph style from the page theme; splash-shown is answered and deliberately does nothing, because the launch screen is a themed window background Android replaces on first frame.",
      "adds": {
        "android": [
          "set-appearance",
          "splash-shown"
        ],
